{"id":"sun","name":"Sun","aliases":["Sun"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:sun","torrey:sun-the"],"groups":["Miracles concerning"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Sun","text":"(Heb. shemesh), first mentioned along with the moon as the two great luminaries of heaven (Gen. 1:14-18). By their motions and influence they were intended to mark and divide times and seasons. The worship of the sun was one of the oldest forms of false religion (Job 31:26, 27), and was common among the Egyptians and Chaldeans and other pagan nations. The Jews were warned against this form of idolatry (Deut. 4:19; 17:3; comp. 2 Kings 23:11; Jer. 19:13)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8121","lemma":"שֶׁמֶשׁ","xlit":"shemesh","gloss":"the sun","kjv":"east side, sun, west, window. See also H1053","count":48,"share":0.44},{"strong":"G2246","lemma":"ἥλιος","xlit":"hḗlios","gloss":"perhaps akin to the alternate of G138 )","kjv":"+ east, sun","count":20,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H3394","lemma":"יָרֵחַ","xlit":"yârêach","gloss":"the moon","kjv":"moon. Yrechow. See H3405","count":18,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H216","lemma":"אוֹר","xlit":"ʼôwr","gloss":"illumination or luminary","kjv":"bright, clear, day, light","count":15,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H3556","lemma":"כּוֹכָב","xlit":"kôwkâb","gloss":"a star","kjv":"star","count":11,"share":0.1},{"strong":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","xlit":"shâmayim","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, astrologer, heaven","count":15,"share":0.14}],"verses":["Gen.19.23","Gen.28.11","Gen.37.9","Exod.16.21","Deut.4.19","Deut.4.41","Deut.17.3","Deut.24.13","Deut.33.14","Josh.10.12","Josh.10.13","Josh.12.1","Judg.5.31","Judg.9.33","2Sam.12.11","2Sam.12.12","2Sam.23.4","2Kgs.23.5","2Kgs.23.11","Ps.19.4","Ps.50.1","Ps.74.16","Ps.84.11","Ps.104.19","Ps.113.3","Ps.121.6","Ps.136.8","Ps.148.3","Eccl.1.5","Eccl.11.7","Song.1.6","Isa.13.10","Isa.38.8","Isa.45.6","Isa.49.10","Isa.60.20","Jer.8.2","Jer.15.9","Jer.31.35","Ezek.8.16","Ezek.32.7","Joel.2.10","Joel.2.31","Joel.3.1